# Gate step 1614-5x7m — the preflight door's deadline and grace are wall clock,
# not a count of polls. build.sh's _pf_now and _pf_run_guard are extracted at
# run time and run against a planted TERM-ignoring guard under a 2 s deadline:
# the fixed door kills it within 4 s plain, with slowed polls, and under
# taskpolicy -b (darwin); the poll-counting pre-fix door overruns in the same run.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the preflight door's wall-clock deadline (1614-5x7m)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-preflight-wall-clock-deadline.lua"
STEP_ERROR="the preflight door's deadline no longer holds by wall clock (1614-5x7m) — see the FAIL lines above"
STEP_OK="Preflight wall-clock deadline fixture passed"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="tlatoanis-macbook-air 2026-10-11 darwin ok:preflight-wall-clock-deadline:6 arms"
# ORDER 2155-gpar: runs alone, never beside a sibling step in the gate pool.
STEP_SERIAL="watches the shared timing or metrics log, or runs a nested gate"
STEP_LANES="timing"
# ORDER 2157-ginp: the paths this step reads, RECORDED ONLY (not yet used to
# skip it; that waits on an operator ruling). First cut: the step's own script
# plus every repo path it names literally.
STEP_INPUTS="scripts/lua/test-preflight-wall-clock-deadline.lua"
